  "recommendation_text": "### Recommended model (recommended)\n\n**MCA (14 dimensions) + K-Means with k = 2**, yielding **2 clusters** (sizes: C0 = 607, C1 = 524).\n\n**Evidence**\n\n- Stability: mean resampling ARI 0.94 (SD 0.05); least stable cluster mean Jaccard 0.97.\n- Separation: Gower silhouette 0.200 (no substantial structure); mean response-profile association (Cram\u00e9r's V) 0.43.\n- Coverage 100%; balance 1.00; gates passed 5/5.\n- Robustness: top-ranked in 100% of 5,000 random weightings (**robust**).\n- Cross-family agreement: mean pairwise ARI 0.16 across the candidate partitions.\n\n**Why not the others**\n\n- K-Modes: eligible but ranked lower (score 0.10 vs 0.90).\n- Agglomerative: failed G4, G5 (resampling ARI \u2265 0.60; worst-cluster Jaccard \u2265 0.60).\n- HDBSCAN: no qualifying representative in Notebook 03 (see its admissibility criteria).\n\n**Reading this recommendation honestly**\n\n- The Gower silhouette indicates no substantial separation: respondents form overlapping gradients of response patterns rather than distinct types. The clusters are useful summaries, not natural categories.\n- Clusters describe aggregate response patterns in a 2016, voluntary, self-selected, largely tech-sector sample; they are not clinical labels, risk scores or employee classifications.",
